From ce9bb074dcc2086204a6175d6432cfdc7fc1d687 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Norton <gregory@serenade.local>
Date: Sat, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/10] WindowServer: Support booting on host systems

Several startup steps assume Serenity kernel facilities that do not exist
on host systems. Make them tolerant instead of fatal:

- Skip the TTY graphics-mode switch (Serenity-only ioctl).
- Allow overriding the config file path via $WINDOW_SERVER_CONFIG.
- Resolve themes, icons, and cursor assets through a res_root() helper
  that honors $SERENITY_RES.
- Only watch input devicemap directories and /etc/Keyboard.ini when they
  exist; there is no kernel keymap to read on hosts.
- Add Screen::take_screenshot() (a copy of the front buffer) and an
  optional SIGUSR1 handler that dumps it as PNG to $WINDOW_SERVER_SCREENSHOT,
  for headless testing.

